An unofficial port, not made by The Document Foundation. "LibreOffice" and its logos are
trademarks of The Document Foundation. The LibreOffice program itself is installed unmodified,
as published by The Document Foundation.

Icons (icons/): LibreOffice's own application icons, unmodified, from the
libreoffice26.8-debian-menus package of the same release, Mozilla Public License 2.0.

Downloaded on first use, not included in the package:
  LibreOffice 26.8.2 for Linux aarch64 (Debian packages), (C) The Document Foundation and
  contributors, Mozilla Public License 2.0, from
  https://downloadarchive.documentfoundation.org/libreoffice/old/26.8.2.2/deb/aarch64/
  Its own licence files are installed with it under
  ~/.local/share/libreoffice.juujbyg/libreoffice/opt/libreoffice26.8/

Included in the package (lib/), unmodified, from Ubuntu's archive:
  libmaliit-glib (maliit-framework 2.3.0) and im-maliit.so (maliit-inputcontext-gtk
  0.99.1+git20260515+faf373b), GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later.
  Source: http://ports.ubuntu.com/ubuntu-ports/pool/universe/m/maliit-framework/ and
  http://ports.ubuntu.com/ubuntu-ports/pool/universe/m/maliit-inputcontext-gtk/

The theme in share/themes/LibreTouch builds on GTK's Adwaita theme (LGPL-2.1+), which it
loads from the system's GTK library rather than copying.
